Original commit body from 1163bfa:

Expand semantic entry detection to recognize additional concept types from
FRAMEWORK_PATTERNS enrichment. This enables higher-confidence entrypoint
detection based on actual framework patterns rather than path heuristics.

New concept types detected:
- controller -> EntrypointKind.CONTROLLER (generic controller)
- task -> EntrypointKind.BACKGROUND_TASK (async/background jobs)
- scheduled_task -> EntrypointKind.SCHEDULED_TASK (cron jobs)
- websocket_handler/websocket_gateway -> EntrypointKind.WEBSOCKET_HANDLER
- event_handler -> EntrypointKind.EVENT_HANDLER
- command -> EntrypointKind.CLI_COMMAND
- liveview -> EntrypointKind.CONTROLLER (Phoenix LiveView)
- graphql_resolver/graphql_schema -> EntrypointKind.GRAPHQL_SERVER

Key changes:
- Add 5 new EntrypointKind enum values for concept-based detection
- Expand _detect_from_concepts() to handle all entrypoint-worthy concepts
- Framework-aware labels when framework info is available in concept
- Deduplicate entries when same kind appears multiple times
- Add comprehensive tests for all new concept types

Benefits:
- Higher confidence (0.95) based on actual decorator/pattern matching
- Eliminates false positives (e.g., React Router won't have route concepts)
- Framework-aware labels improve user understanding
- Gradual migration path with path heuristics as fallback (Option A)
